# Reserved-term list : example / template.
#
# Copy this file to ".reserved-terms" (which is gitignored) and fill it
# with the internal-only terms the pre-publish scan should flag if they ever
# appear in the public tree: internal naming, earlier experiment / codename
# references, non-public hostnames, and non-public contact strings. One ERE
# (extended regex) term per line. Blank lines and lines starting with "#"
# are ignored. The scanner ORs the terms together, case-insensitively.
#
# Why this is not committed: keeping the list in tracked source would
# publish the very terms it exists to keep out of the public tree. Holding
# it here (gitignored) or in the OR_RESERVED_TERMS CI secret lets the
# check run without publishing the list. Outside contributors run the
# scanner with this list empty and never see the internal terms.
#
# The entries below are PLACEHOLDERS, replace them.

# Internal naming / reserved words (whole-word):
\b(ProjectAlpha|ProjectBeta)\b

# Earlier experiment / codename references:
\b(LegacyExperimentName)\b

# Non-public hostnames:
internal-host\.example|build-host\.example|myhost\.local

# Non-public domains:
@(example-internal\.com|example-internal\.net)
